From 6b3d5c7e23cb7e702477a3af1ca81c6e1d48339e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 03:12:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(od-sevev): the vote stops the clock under the
 election card
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

While O3 is open and unconfirmed the round holds: no ultimatum counts
down or expires, no demand ages, no join, transfer, card or court tick,
and the economy pauses too, so the card is a pause and never a farm.
The seats the player opened the card with are the seats they vote on.

Politics.tick(ctx.vote) + Politics.holds_for_vote in the sim;
main.gd vote_open() drives it. Spec §7.4 with the measured slip table
(15 of 72 median-player gates fell within 30 s on the card before).
Tests: test_vote_hold.gd (sim), test_modals (scene), bench V1 (every
leader and deal keeps the gate after 30 s on the card).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JZ6f2h5tcXVKGAwuAga5z8
