From 14778153a516256fb8639f07e0d35fb87646d37d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 05:25:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(od-sevev): a coalition pill never trades seats down
 (Bennett's trap)

Won't-sit-with (excludes) now holds both ways with the bigger side
(seats + abstain/2) first: the smaller side does not ask while the
bigger sits and its open offer closes when the bigger comes in; the
bigger may come back and sends the smaller out. Before, Gafni's or
Abbas's join silently threw Liberman's 12 seats out of Bennett's round
with no rejoin pill: a player who pays every pill never held 61 in 5
of 9 deals, and picker_web's Bennett round never did either.

Liberman no longer excludes Abbas: they sat together in 2021 (fact
raam-2021, Abbas's own line in Bennett's round). Bibi's round is
unchanged except that Abbas's rejoin pill closes when Ben Gvir returns.
Medians: Bennett 8:03 (was 8:08), Eisenkot 8:10 (was 8:50), Golan 7:59.

