tools/web/round_play.mjs: the loop both drivers use. It pays the chat
first and saves for an open ultimatum, re-reads odDev before every tap
burst, taps the live CTA centre (odDev.ctaAt; the stored lowerY went
stale when the layout split again), checks the vote hold on the open
card (runSec and seats unchanged for 1.5 s), and logs any real
navigation with the page's own history calls. Speed 5 (was 10/12),
budgets 1500/1800 s wall for a loaded machine; the long press holds
until the leader card is up.

The mid-run navigation is the game's LayerHistory: a layer closes
(history.go(-1), async), another opens before the traversal lands, the
traversal skips the new entry, and the next close goes back past the
root and leaves the page. The drivers wait for the traversal (settle)
before acting; the game fix is the developer's.

dev_probe: coal {lines, afford, ultLeft, save, vote} and ctaAt.
Spec §7.2.2 and §7.4 filled in with the measured tables.

